The core components of Linux (kernel, user space, init/systemd)

core components of linux  are  hardware- kernal - shell - applications

hardware includes cpu ram keyboard etc
kernel is the core component of linux which manages and talk to hardware and operations and system processes 
shell: it is a command line interface thet interprates codes line by line and  executes user commands
sys libraries it is a set of functions that help application interact with linux kernal 
sys utilities :these are essential command line commands that helps to troubleshoot, manage resource and monitoring


How processes are created and managed
types of process 
>created:the process id being created
>ready: its already created and ready to run
>running: its runnung 
>waiting:its waiting for its chance to run 
stopped:process is paused by user and it is stopped
>terminated process is terminated all its resources has been removed/cleaned up
>zombie: its child process is executed but its parrent process dosent has chance to read its exit
>orphan:its parrent process is terminated and child process is still running 


What systemd does and why it matters
systemd is the core software that boots linux system it runs as pid 1 and it start stops the service
It runs from the starting of the os it manages services such as start stops daemons (ie background task like web server)
it can run multiple processes at a time hence it is fast.
monitors processes handles log from entire system
